<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Racial segregation</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Racial segregation is the enforced separation of people of different races in housing, public life and rights. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> codified racial segregation in its African colonies through a series of laws, particularly after the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. These measures were designed to preserve Italian dominance over the colonised populations.</p></div>
